s GitHub App auth. Host-mode jobs can reach `~/.ard/sidecars`, but it holds no credential. Host-mode jobs run as the controller's uid: they can read the GitHub App key and `~/.config/gh` by absolute path, write the controller's clone, and undo `chmod a-w`. Host mode is allowed for every role ([#84](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/84)), but a role that reads untrusted input (every triage, worker and reviewer role, and an LLM scanner) warns loudly when it has no `Dockerfile`; deterministic scanners are exempt, and nothing warns under `executor: k8s`, where every job runs in a container. `ard config check` and the first successful config load of `ard serve` (and any role a later config adds) log one `executor.host_untrusted` WARN per such role and also write it to stderr, so it survives `--log-level`. The local executor logs the WARN again for every host-mode job of such a role and appends a `host_untrusted` row to the `events` table. **Default agent image under the local executor (#244, part of #55).** `ard serve` and `ard config check` read the host setting `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`: a digest-pinned reference (`<name>@sha256:<64 hex>`) or a local image ID (`sha256:<hex>` from `make agent-image`); tags are refused (`executor.CheckImageRef`, `ErrImageRef`), and an invalid value stops startup. When it is set, `Prepare` runs every job that reads untrusted input and has no `Dockerfile` (triage, worker agent, test and fix steps, reviewer, and LLM scanner jobs) under Docker in that image, with the same flags and mounts as a Dockerfile role (`--cap-drop ALL`, `no-new-privileges`, worktree at `/work`, role directory `:ro`, and so on). A role's own `Dockerfile` wins. Deterministic scanners (trusted input) stay on the host. A local image is used as is; a digest that is not present is pulled. There is no fallback to host mode: `ard serve` runs `docker version` at startup and fails if Docker is down, and a job whose Docker setup fails at `Prepare` fails there. The controller's clone is not mounted, so `git` has no repository inside the container; every Docker job gets `GOFLAGS=-buildvcs=false` so `go build` does not fail on VCS stamping. Unset keeps today's behaviour. With it set, `ard config check` and `ard serve` no longer log or record `executor.host_untrusted` for roles it covers, and the hint of the warning names `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`. Each warning lists what the job can reach, including `~/.ard` (state, config snapshots, the pause file, other jobs' worktrees and logs). The owner accepts this risk while ard runs only on owner-controlled repos, and revisits it when moving to the spark cluster, where every job runs in a container once the k8s executor (#54) lands. Until then the Gate 1 dry-run soak on spark (see Rollout and Delivery) runs `ard serve` with the local executor in a pod, and the deterministic cve scanner runs there as a host subprocess of the controller container: its role directory has no `Dockerfile`, and the `ard` image carries its pinned tools. Only deterministic scanners run in that pod: it starts `ard serve --loops scanners,stale,reaper` ([#187](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/187)), so the triage, worker and reviewer loops never run there, even though `.ard/config.yaml` on `main` has agent roles. `--loops` takes a comma-separated list of loop names (scanners, stale, triage, workers, reviewers, reviewfix, merger, janitor, reaper, budget; `budget` is the status-issue notice loop, the claim gate is always on), defaults to every loop, and rejects an unknown name with exit 2. `ard serve` and `ard config check` refuse to run on git older than 2.47.0, because the committer's fetches fail on older versions.\n \n A worker job is several executor jobs (`<id>`, `<id>t1`, `<id>f1`, ...) under one state job and one slot; the Reaper watches whichever step is stored on the job, so its heartbeat and deadline rules apply to tests too.\n \ndiff --git a/internal/github/auth.go b/internal/github/auth.go\nindex 7baafb6..2395e5d 100644\n--- a/internal/github/auth.go\n+++ b/internal/github/auth.go\n@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ type AppAuth struct {\n \tbaseURL string\n \trepo    Repo\n \tinst    *ghinstallation.Transport\n+\tinstID  int64 // configured or discovered installation id\n }\n \n // configure is called by New with the repo and API base URL.\n@@ -113,6 +114,7 @@ func (a *AppAuth) installation(ctx context.Context) (*ghinstallation.Transport,\n \t\t\treturn nil, err\n \t\t}\n \t}\n+\ta.instID = id\n \tt, err := ghinstallation.New(base, a.AppID, id, a.PrivateKey)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"github: app transport: %w\", err)\n@@ -126,6 +128,22 @@ func (a *AppAuth) installation(ctx context.Context) (*ghinstallation.Transport,\n \treturn t, nil\n }\n \n+// installationID returns the installation id, discovering it when unknown.\n+func (a *AppAuth) installationID(ctx context.Context) (int64, error) {\n+\ta.mu.Lock()\n+\tid := a.instID\n+\ta.mu.Unlock()\n+\tif id != 0 {\n+\t\treturn id, nil\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := a.installation(ctx); err != nil {\n+\t\treturn 0, err\n+\t}\n+\ta.mu.Lock()\n+\tdefer a.mu.Unlock()\n+\treturn a.instID, nil\n+}\n+\n func (a *AppAuth) discover(ctx context.Context, base http.RoundTripper) (int64, error) {\n \tif a.repo == (Repo{}) {\n \t\treturn 0, errors.New(\"github: cannot discover installation without a repo\")\ndiff --git a/internal/github/scoped.go b/internal/github/scoped.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..430669a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/github/scoped.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@\n+package github\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"io\"\n+\t\"log/slog\"\n+\t\"net/http\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+// ErrCannotScope means the credentials cannot mint scoped tokens.\n+var ErrCannotScope = errors.New(\"github: a personal access token cannot be scoped down; the k8s executor needs GitHub App auth\")\n+\n+// ErrNotInInstallation means a requested repository is not covered by the\n+// App installation.\n+var ErrNotInInstallation = errors.New(\"github: repository is not in the app installation\")\n+\n+// ScopedToken is a short-lived installation token. Its value never reaches a\n+// log or an error message through fmt or slog.\n+type ScopedToken struct {\n+\tValue     string\n+\tExpiresAt time.Time\n+}\n+\n+const redactedToken = \"[token]\"\n+\n+// String hides the value.\n+func (ScopedToken) String() string { return redactedToken }\n+\n+// GoString hides the value for %#v.\n+func (ScopedToken) GoString() string { return redactedToken }\n+\n+// LogValue hides the value from slog.\n+func (ScopedToken) LogValue() slog.Value { return slog.StringValue(redactedToken) }\n+\n+// ScopedMinter returns a as an *AppAuth, or ErrCannotScope for any other kind.\n+func ScopedMinter(a Auth) (*AppAuth, error) {\n+\tif app, ok := a.(*AppAuth); ok && app != nil {\n+\t\treturn app, nil\n+\t}\n+\treturn nil, ErrCannotScope\n+}\n+\n+func (a *AppAuth) apiBase() (http.RoundTripper, string) {\n+\ta.mu.Lock()\n+\tdefer a.mu.Unlock()\n+\tbase := a.base\n+\tif base == nil {\n+\t\tbase = http.DefaultTransport\n+\t}\n+\tu := a.baseURL\n+\tif u == \"\" {\n+\t\tu = defaultBaseURL\n+\t}\n+\treturn base, strings.TrimRight(u, \"/\")\n+}\n+\n+// MintReadToken mints an installation token limited to contents:read on repos.\n+// Every repo must belong to the installation's owner; otherwise no request is made.\n+func (a *AppAuth) MintReadToken(ctx context.Context, repos []Repo) (ScopedToken, error) {\n+\tif len(repos) == 0 {\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, errors.New(\"github: no repositories to scope the token to\")\n+\t}\n+\ta.mu.Lock()\n+\towner := a.repo.Owner\n+\ta.mu.Unlock()\n+\tnames := make([]string, 0, len(repos))\n+\tfor _, r := range repos {\n+\t\tif r.Name == \"\" || !strings.EqualFold(r.Owner, owner) {\n+\t\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", ErrNotInInstallation, r)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tnames = append(names, r.Name)\n+\t}\n+\tid, err := a.installationID(ctx)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, err\n+\t}\n+\tbase, root := a.apiBase()\n+\tjwt, err := a.appsTransport(base)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, err\n+\t}\n+\tpayload, err := json.Marshal(map[string]any{\n+\t\t\"repositories\": names,\n+\t\t\"permissions\":  map[string]string{\"contents\": \"read\"},\n+\t})\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, err\n+\t}\n+\turl := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s/app/installations/%d/access_tokens\", root, id)\n+\treq, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodPost, url, bytes.NewReader(payload))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, err\n+\t}\n+\treq.Header.Set(\"Accept\", \"application/vnd.github+json\")\n+\treq.Header.Set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n+\tresp, err := newAPIClient(jwt).Do(req)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, fmt.Errorf(\"github: mint scoped token: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\n+\tbody, _ := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(resp.Body, 1<<20))\n+\tswitch resp.StatusCode {\n+\tcase http.StatusCreated:\n+\tcase http.StatusUnprocessableEntity:\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", ErrNotInInstallation, errorMessage(body))\n+\tdefault:\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, fmt.Errorf(\"github: mint scoped token: %w\", statusError(resp.StatusCode, body))\n+\t}\n+\tvar out struct {\n+\t\tToken     string    `json:\"token\"`\n+\t\tExpiresAt time.Time `json:\"expires_at\"`\n+\t}\n+\tif err := json.Unmarshal(body, &out); err != nil || out.Token == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn ScopedToken{}, errors.New(\"github: mint scoped token: unexpected response\")\n+\t}\n+\treturn ScopedToken{Value: out.Token, ExpiresAt: out.ExpiresAt}, nil\n+}\n+\n+// RevokeToken revokes an installation token. An already revoked or expired\n+// token (401) counts as success.\n+func (a *AppAuth) RevokeToken(ctx context.Context, tok string) error {\n+\tbase, root := a.apiBase()\n+\treq, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodDelete, root+\"/installation/token\", nil)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn err\n+\t}\n+\treq.Header.Set(\"Accept\", \"application/vnd.github+json\")\n+\treq.Header.Set(\"Authorization\", \"Bearer \"+tok)\n+\tresp, err := newAPIClient(base).Do(req)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"github: revoke token: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\n+\tbody, _ := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(resp.Body, 1<<20))\n+\tswitch resp.StatusCode {\n+\tcase http.StatusNoContent, http.StatusUnauthorized:\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"github: revoke token: %w\", statusError(resp.StatusCode, body))\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/github/scoped_test.go b/internal/github/scoped_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..8fad867\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/github/scoped_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@\n+package github\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"log/slog\"\n+\t\"net/http\"\n+\t\"net/http/httptest\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"sync/atomic\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+)\n+\n+const scopedSecretValue = \"scoped-value-for-tests\"\n+\n+func scopedApp(t *testing.T, h http.HandlerFunc) (*AppAuth, *atomic.Int32) {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\tvar n atomic.Int32\n+\tsrv := httptest.NewServer(http.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n+\t\tn.Add(1)\n+\t\th(w, r)\n+\t}))\n+\tt.Cleanup(srv.Close)\n+\ta := &AppAuth{AppID: 12, InstallationID: 34, PrivateKey: []byte(testKeyPEM(t))}\n+\ta.configure(Repo{\"o\", \"r\"}, srv.URL)\n+\treturn a, &n\n+}\n+\n+func TestMintReadToken(t *testing.T) {\n+\ttests := []struct {\n+\t\tname     string\n+\t\trepos    []Repo\n+\t\thandler  http.HandlerFunc\n+\t\twantErr  error\n+\t\tanyErr   bool\n+\t\trequests int32\n+\t}{\n+\t\t{name: \"created\", repos: []Repo{{\"o\", \"r\"}, {\"o\", \"side\"}}, requests: 1, handler: func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {\n+\t\t\tif r.Method != http.MethodPost || r.URL.Path != \"/app/installations/34/access_tokens\" {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"request = %s %s\", r.Method, r.URL.Path)\n+\